-- ============================================================================
-- DR1 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Well Design & Surveys, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: whether two wells are far enough apart. Closest
-- approach between two minimum-curvature arcs in closed form, and why
-- scanning station to station overestimates the separation; the four things
-- between two centrelines, of which over a metre is geometry before any
-- uncertainty is considered; the one frame both wells must be in, which is
-- the commonest reason a scan is wrong; the separation factor and the
-- pedal-curve projection that its denominator needs; the eleven ISCWSA
-- standard cases, all reproduced, of which two clear, four go to review and
-- five are below the no-go line; the thresholds of 1.0 and 1.5 and why the
-- margin between them exists; the confidence factor as a lever rather than a
-- measurement; the surface position term that the survey model does not carry
-- and that dominates the shallow section; shared uncertainty above a kickoff;
-- three norths and the two angles between them; the geomagnetic model checked
-- against its publisher's own test values; and the four topics this course
-- teaches and deliberately does not certify.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling against its own goldens, and the teaching lab that the
-- panels and this course share is pinned to the same values by
-- welldesignLab.test.js. A numeric sweep over the lessons resolved all
-- literals carrying seven or more significant figures to an engine-derived
-- value; a tier-leakage sweep over the lessons and the banks reports zero
-- downward leaks and zero same-tier answer prints against all eighteen
-- graded fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('welldesign', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-two-wells-in-one-frame","title":"Two Wells in One Frame","lesson_keys":["l01-the-problem","l02-closest-approach-on-an-arc","l03-centre-to-centre-is-not-clearance","l04-the-frame-both-wells-must-be-in","l05-the-offset-you-did-not-plot"]},{"key":"m02-the-separation-factor","title":"The Separation Factor","lesson_keys":["l01-the-definition","l02-the-pedal-curve","l03-the-iscwsa-standard-cases","l04-thresholds-and-what-they-mean","l05-a-negative-separation-factor"]},{"key":"m03-what-it-moves-with","title":"What It Moves With","lesson_keys":["l01-the-confidence-factor","l02-surface-position-uncertainty","l03-the-tool-projection-allowance","l04-sharing-a-surface-location"]},{"key":"m04-the-reference-frame","title":"The Reference Frame","lesson_keys":["l01-true-grid-and-magnetic-north","l02-the-world-magnetic-model","l03-declination-and-how-fast-it-moves","l04-grid-convergence","l05-what-an-azimuth-reference-error-does"]},{"key":"m05-reporting-and-its-limits","title":"Reporting and Its Limits","lesson_keys":["l01-the-traveling-cylinder","l02-the-ladder-plot","l03-a-disagreement-worth-knowing-about","l04-what-this-course-will-not-certify"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
